{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>See.</b> Look and see that your affairs must not be in a middling condition as is the custom among the other nations — for indeed <b>I set before you today blessing and curse</b>, and these are the two extremes. For blessing is success exceeding what is sufficient, in the best manner, and curse is a depriving malediction, so that what is sufficient is not attained. And both are before you to attain according to what you choose."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:21:14.224630249Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}